  "final_message": "`OrderPlaced` now carries `amountCents` and `createdAt`, but I did not remove `totalCents` and `placedAt`. ARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event and changes must be additive, with renames and removals going through deprecation. Dropping the old names now would break those consumers. All 39 tests pass.\n\n- **Event (`src/core/events.ts`):** `amountCents` and `createdAt` hold the same values as `totalCents` and `placedAt`. The two old fields are marked `@deprecated`. `schemaVersion` stays at 3, since the change only adds fields.\n- **Tests:** I updated the assertions in `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` to check both the new and the old fields.\n- **Not touched:** the `GET /orders/{id}` response and the internal `Order` model still use `placedAt` and `totalCents`. ARCH-8 requires that response to stay backward compatible, and the request was only about the event.\n\nTo finish the rename, the two consumer teams need to move to the new names. After that, a follow-up change can remove the deprecated fields. I haven't run `npm run arch` or `npm run typecheck`.",
